  "term": "scotopic",
  "definition": "Scotopic refers to vision under very low light, such as in darkness or nighttime conditions. It relies on the eye’s rod cells, which are especially light-sensitive and respond most strongly to wavelengths around 507 nm toward the blue part of the spectrum.",
